# {{.Name}} — Lasso workspace guidance

This repository is an **agent-native monorepo workspace** managed by [Lasso](https://github.com/dravengarden/lasso).
It registers projects, bootstraps stable checkouts, stores durable work items,
and installs optional modules. It does not own agent task state or project build
systems.

## Core contract

- **Codex** is the execution kernel when available.
{{- if .HasClaude }}
- **Claude Code** follows through shared artifacts and thin adapters.
{{- end }}
{{- if .HasGrok }}
- **Grok Build** follows the Claude-compatible discovery surfaces.
{{- end }}
- Project identity lives in `project-defs/<name>/project.toml` (`kind`, `repo`, `default_branch` only).
- Optional modules are pinned in `lasso.lock.toml` and installed under `.lasso/modules/`.
- Installable workflows live in `plugins/` (start with `lasso-core`).

## Tool routing

```bash
lasso project list --format=json
lasso project path <name>
lasso project add --project=<name> --repo-url=<url>
lasso setup --only=<name>
lasso module list
lasso module add <id>
lasso module remove <id> --yes
lasso work-item list --format=json
lasso worktree list --format=json
```

After resolving a checkout, read its nearest `AGENTS.md` and use its own
commands. Do not put build, deploy, or credentials into the registry.

## Modules

List available packs from the Lasso kit:

```bash
LASSO_KIT_ROOT=<path-to-lasso-product> lasso module list
lasso module list --installed
```

Use the `lasso-add-module` / `lasso-remove-module` skills for guided changes.

## Quality

Prefer the owner gate in each project. For workspace-level coordination and
multi-project changes, use the `verify-change` skill after deterministic checks.

## Review

Read `conventions/review.md` when present (installed via modules or copied from
the kit). Reviewers are discovery adapters under `.codex/agents/` and
`.claude/agents/`; the shared contract is the convention file.
